   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "וְאֵין מִסְתַּפְּרִין מֵהֶן בְּכׇל מָקוֹם. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: יִשְׂרָאֵל הַמִּסְתַּפֵּר מִגּוֹי רוֹאֶה בַּמַּרְאָה, וְגוֹי הַמִּסְתַּפֵּר מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל, כֵּיוָן שֶׁהִגִּיעַ לִבְלוֹרִיתוֹ שׁוֹמֵט אֶת יָדוֹ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «And one may not have his hair cut by» gentiles «anywhere. The Sages taught» in a baraita: «A Jew who has his hair cut by a gentile» should «observe» the gentile’s actions «in a mirror» while he cuts his hair. «And» in the case of «a gentile who has his hair cut by a Jew, when» the Jew «reaches» the gentile’s «forelock he removes his hand» and does not cut it, because it is associated with idol worship."
  }
